    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Xylem conducts water and minerals unidirectionally from roots to leaves, whereas Phloem transports food bidirectionally.",
        "Ethylene is the only natural plant hormone that exists in a gaseous state and promotes fruit ripening.",
        "Light reactions of photosynthesis take place in the Grana of chloroplasts, while dark reactions occur in the Stroma.",
        "Vegetative propagation occurs through specialized plant parts: stem tubers in Potato, runners in Grass, and foliar buds in Bryophyllum."
      ],
      "id": "ndpjd99"
    },
